WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.462 --> 00:00:06.170
BEN LITHGOW SMITH:
Deutsche Bank provides

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:08.510
a suite of products
and services across

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:12.330
retail and private banking,
corporate transaction banking,

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.420
lending, and asset
and wealth management.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:16.400
DEEPAK SAREEN: So DevOps
and Cloud adoption

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.890
are part of our
technology transformation,

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:21.080
and the DevOps Research
and Assessment,

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.012
in short, the DORA
assessment, is key to this.

00:00:23.012 --> 00:00:24.470
BEN LITHGOW SMITH:
And the business

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:27.860
challenges that we
face, really around cost

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.140
and also looking to increase
our in-house engineering

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.038
capability.

00:00:31.038 --> 00:00:33.080
DEEPAK SAREEN: While we
previously relied heavily

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.940
on external
developers, we are now

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:37.940
strengthening our internal
engineering capabilities.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:41.060
The key technology
goals for this project

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:44.270
were to reduce risk,
complexity, and cost

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.190
while supporting the
business innovation

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.440
and growth by
enabling new products

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.210
and services for our customers.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.180
To this end, we are looking
to fully automate development,

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:54.870
deployment, and controls.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:58.013
Enhanced DevOps practices
are central to this approach.

00:00:58.013 --> 00:00:59.930
BEN LITHGOW SMITH: The
impact of these changes

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:02.450
started immediately and
improved steadily, particularly

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:06.170
for release frequency, which
rose from one release per month

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.710
in January 2021 to
three releases per month

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.690
by November 2021.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:14.420
Stability also improved,
the number of incidents

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.592
declining by 40%
in the same time.

00:01:16.592 --> 00:01:18.050
DEEPAK SAREEN: An
initial challenge

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:20.750
we faced was that the full
DORA assessment was being

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.950
re-platformed and
wasn't available,

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.730
so instead, we worked
closely with Google

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:28.310
to co-create a lightweight
assessment involving

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:30.800
approximately 50
participants across the band

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.625
to demonstrate the usefulness.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:35.000
BEN LITHGOW SMITH: We then
selected an initial pilot area

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.070
for a full assessment,
and Googlers

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:39.770
were instrumental in helping
to select the granularity

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:41.840
to run that pilot
out and supporting

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.660
with initial briefings
and the result's debriefs.

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:47.570
We also had regular working
sessions with our partners

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:50.690
at Google as we scaled
things to workshop ideas

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:52.760
and plan next steps
together with a lot

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.420
of asynchronous collaboration
as well with Google partners

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.312
and the DORA team specifically.

00:01:58.312 --> 00:02:00.020
The pilot gave us
great insights into how

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:02.360
we could run DORA at scale
across Deutsche Bank, which

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:05.600
we took into the first
full divisional rollout.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.653
This also showed the need for
an option for teams too small

00:02:08.653 --> 00:02:10.070
for the full
assessment, which led

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.410
us to develop and facilitate
a quick check along

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:15.860
with trying to train our
approach for scaling delivery.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:18.860
We're really thankful to
receive this award from Google

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.200
and to all the teams who've
participated in the DORA

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.720
assessments across
the DB and have really

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:27.240
helped to facilitate real
transformational change.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:30.450
We're also really thankful
for our Google partners,

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:34.580
both on our account and with
the Google DORA team as well.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:37.330
[MUSIC PLAYING]

